 #:seon.task{:name "definition-identity-is-derived-from-the-runtime-value-type"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Whether an evaluated Var is a program definition is decided by program-value? (fn? root or :test metadata, with the absent-intern sentinel), while publication decides by clj-kondo's seon.fn/function-definition? (every def, defonce, defmulti). Live on default pid 89341: kondo gives entities for (def m {:a 1}), (def a (atom 0)), (defmulti mm :k) and (def g (partial + 1)); program-value? says false, false, false, true. So a data def is a program entity from a file and a private binding at the REPL, and the unindexed-change text's point-free example is stale (kondo matches it; it is refused as uncontracted). One authority: the analyzed entities, looked up by name, with one predicate shared by files and REPL."
             :must-read #{seon.sci.eval/program-value? seon.sci.eval/program-definitions seon.sci.eval/program-change seon.fn/function-definition?}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/eval-path-audit-2026-09-26.md"}}
